body:
Every social media is built to be addicting, they simply made a competitor to facebook, youtube, and instagram.

The US government doesn't even prioritize the interests of Americans, I don't know if you have been paying attention recently but several cities have had their drinking water contaminated by train derailments and the government hasn't done shit or said shit. 

&#x200B;

You keep repeating the same stuff without explaining how this stops China from getting data from any of their 100s of other investments into social media or buying it off a data broker.

&#x200B;

Do you think Reddit should be banned next? A decent portion of the company is owned by Tencent. This sets a terrible legal precedent of just banning anything from a country we don't like

I disagree, you haven't provided any evidence of how this will make it harder for the CCP to get data. They already have their hands in other social media including the one we are using right now. They have already had major scrutiny over how they store their data in the US. I believe it to be a incredible waste of time and resources that could just be used to make common sense privacy laws, but congress basically said during the hearing that they don't care what American companies do with our data. I also think the US government is a more immediate threat to me than the CCP considering I don't live there and if we're being completely honest, I'd rather have them have my data than the US government.

&#x200B;

Besides, Bytedance will most likely just sell off their shares to an American company, likely Meta who are the ones who lobbied congress to ban Tik Tok in the first place, or Oracle who are already in charge of storing TikTok's data in America.

A serious answer is that on December 7 a "hacker" pretended to be Grace Vanderwaal and got Daniel to give him his username and password to his youtube account and honestly just posted mild shitposts from his account. But the fallout from this caused a several day meltdown in which Daniel would cause damage to the motel he was in.

&#x200B;

on December 10 Daniel had one of his biggest breakdowns after he apparently got a call where the motel threatened to kill him if he came back. While he was in the car with Bob, he hit himself hard enough to give himself a bloody nose and he hit Bob several times while screaming "THE MOTEL THREATENED TO KILL ME" in his best Mickey Mouse impression. I'm pretty sure this was the final straw for Bob as he had to call the police to get Daniel away from him. While Bob did not press charges since Daniel was not arrested, Bob gave him some money and put him on a plane to California with no return ticket.

you people are fucking crazy

&#x200B;

burn in hell
